{
  "format": "souls-form-cases/1",
  "about": "eden:rhythm_box (from #1851). Three lanes, kick, snare and hat, of eight steps each, every step a hit or a rest, a tempo of 60, 90 or 120 beats a minute, and whether the loop plays. With empty hands a Soul programs one step (the original took whole lanes as text, `kick=10001000`; here a step and its beat are choices from closed lists) or the tempo, only while stopped ('Stop the loop before editing its rhythm lanes.', 'Stop the loop before changing tempo.'); starts the loop ('The rhythm is already playing; stop it before restarting.'), never an empty one ('Program at least one selected step before starting an empty rhythm.'); and stops it ('The rhythm is already stopped.').",
